I inspected why POST /api/auth/pin-login returned 404 and applied the minimal fix.
Findings
•	AuthController is present at src/NovaBanking.Api/Controllers/AuthController.cs and correctly decorated:
•	[ApiController]
•	[Route("api/[controller]")]
•	Actions use [HttpPost("pin-login")] and [HttpPost("logout")]
•	The controller was compiled into NovaBanking.Api (present in project).
•	Program.cs did not register controllers or map controller routes; the app used minimal endpoints only. Without AddControllers() + MapControllers(), attribute-routed controllers are not reachable, causing 404 for /api/auth/pin-login.
•	No other route prefixes or namespace issues were found.
Minimal fix applied
•	Registered controllers and mapped routes:
•	Added builder.Services.AddControllers();
•	Added app.MapControllers();
Files changed
•	src/NovaBanking.Api/Program.cs (added AddControllers() and app.MapControllers()).
Build
•	dotnet build succeeded (with warnings); no schema or behavior changes to authentication/database code.
Exact route that should now respond
•	POST http://localhost:5146/api/auth/pin-login
No authentication logic was altered beyond registering controllers and mapping routes.
